when porsche first unveiled the panamera  at the 2009 auto shanghai show  the public were astonished die hard  sports car fans rubbed their eyes when  they saw  a four-door luxury class car with a  front-mounted engine  what was the world coming to what was  porsche doing to its image  was the company jettisoning its  traditions and values  four years later porsche is bringing the  second generation of the panamera  onto the market a clear signal that the  boldness of the engineers and designers  has paid off  our test driver reinhold says this grand  turismo model  sold even better than expected porsche  was counting on selling 20  000 of them a year but has been shifting  30 000.  so unit sales since 2009 total more than  100  000 mostly in the united states in china  we'll show you how the panamera has  changed at the front  and back  and it's not just the appearance things  have improved under the hood too  downsizing is the key word when it comes  to what's new about the v6 engine  the result is up to 18 greater fuel  efficiency  than with the v8 in the older 4s model  with a displacement of three leaders  twin turbochargers produce 20 more  horsepower  and 20 newton meters more torque than  the preceding v8  porsche is unleashing 10 different  versions of the panamera simultaneously  all new are two long executive versions  that provide more comfort and legroom in  the back  we checked out the panamera 4s executive  with the new v6 engine  top speed is 286 kilometers an hour  and it accelerates from zero to 100 in  just five seconds  fuel consumption is officially nine  liters per 100 kilometers  the stretch version is 5.17 meters long  and weighs  exactly two tons only a few tweaks have  changed the front  like on the hood's power dome and on the  headlights  the panamera executive is shorter than  its direct competitors  10 centimeters shorter than the long  version of the audi a8 and 5 centimeters  shorter than a regular bmw  7 series  the long panamera's wheelbase has  increased by  15 centimeters and the back doors are  longer too which makes getting into the  back seats a lot more comfortable  the new panamera hasn't changed much  upfront says reinhold  the headlights are rounder the air  intakes bigger  the power dome on the hood and the  rocker panels on the sides are more  striking  but criticism of the old version focused  on the rear so now the back window  is wider and flatter the rear lights are  new  and in particular the license plate has  been lowered  giving the panamera a better appearance  from behind  here's what the rear looks like as a  whole compared with its predecessor  shown here in black on the left  the button to open the rear hatch is  hidden under the rear windshield wiper  the trunk holds between 445 and 1265  liters of luggage  15 centimeters the panamera executive  has grown by 15 centimeters resulting in  more legroom and space to work in for  rear passengers  if the front passenger seat is vacant  you can move that seat forward from  behind  the executive versions cater to buyers  of chauffeured limousines  but these vehicles drivers are in an  enviable position too  the instruments in front of them and to  the sides are within  easy reach convenient are also the front  and rear parking assists  they provide a nice overview in  otherwise unclear parking situations  power controls enable passengers to  individually adjust the separate back  seats for comfort  the panamera 4s executive costs in  excess of 132  000 euros in germany that makes the  stretch version 25 and a half thousand  more expensive  than a normal 4s porsches come at a  price  including gran turismo versions the long  models from the competition the audi  a8l and the bmw 7 series are available  for 50 or 60 000 euros less  you
 

